  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="9">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:WlArt">Wl art</ref> 9</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="9" corresp="#wit-h">Ego prohibeo ut nullus vendat hominem extra patriam super plenam forisfacturam meam.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-h">I forbid anyone to sell a man out of the country, under pain of incurring the full fine for insubordination to me.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="488">Inst Cn II 3</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 3</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:WlArtRetr_1">Wl art retr 1</ref>; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_41">Leis Wl 41</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="409"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_41">Leis Wl 41–41.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 242–243 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
